{
  "$comment": "VAPP-196 (eApps T1, spec docs/spec/apps.md §11): PACKAGE TESTS, one fixture for the TS reference (src/host/tests.ts) and the Rust core (eui_core::host::tests); Swift and Kotlin replay `validate` through validatePackage over the FFI. A package's `tests: [{name, records?, now?, as?, expr | query | action, expect}]` (at most limits.tests): `records` = {<kind>: [rows]} seeding the test's OWN in-memory store (a row = the kind's data, checked against its schema, plus optional `id` (default `<kind>-<n>`, n from 1 per kind) and `author` (default the test's member); every row stamped `now`); `now` = an ISO instant (default defaults.now; the zone is UTC); `as` = the member id the test runs as (default defaults.as: `mine`, `me`); `role` = their team role, member | owner (default defaults.role). eApps R3: the store holds every seeded row, but the test READS only the rows `as` may read under each kind's `policy` (record-policy.json `readable`), and its action's writes are judged by the policy (record-policy.json; a write to a row it may not read = not found): a refusal = {error: `write <i>: <copy>`}; an action's result lists only the rows it may read. Exactly one of: `expr: {expr, vars?}` (CEL; a var `{source: \"records:<kind>?…\"}` = that binding's value over the store, `?query=<name>` expanded; anything else a literal) → the value or {error}; `query: {name, params?}` (a package query over `records:<from>?query=<name>&<params>`) → the records value; `action: {name, params?, data?}` (runAction as `as` at `now`, then the plan's writes applied to the store, new ids `new-<n>`) → {records: {<kind>: [{…data, id, author}] in store order}, sets, calls} or {error}. `matches`: testMatches(expect, got): an object matches by the keys it names (a missing key reads null), recursively; a list item by item with the same length; anything else by JSON equality. `runs`: runPackageTests → [{name, pass, got}]. `validate`: validatePackage of the base `package` with a case's `with` keys replaced: the tests' SHAPE issues first (`/tests…`); a malformed test list runs no test, and nor does a package with any other issue; else every failing test is ONE issue at `/tests/<i>`: `<name>: expected <canonical JSON>, got <canonical JSON>` (got cut at limits.gotMax code points + `…`).",
  "limits": {
    "tests": 50,
    "gotMax": 300
  },
